This patch is needed because Solaris home directories are often NFS-backed, and
SQLite WAL mode can fail during startup when it tries to mmap the `-shm` sidecar.

What it does:
- uses rollback journal mode instead of WAL for Codex state databases on Solaris
- removes stale Solaris WAL sidecars when the WAL file is empty or absent
- uses an exclusive one-shot connection to convert existing WAL-marked databases
  before opening the normal connection pool
- keeps WAL mode unchanged on other targets

Why it is needed:
- without it, Codex can fail at startup on Solaris NFS homes with
  `SQLITE_IOERR_SHMMAP` / SQLite extended error code 5386

